== a new config
  A new config: first the settings for this machine, then a domain.
? client name [<host>] -> laptop
? uploads at once [4] -> 
? chunk buffers [4] -> 
? downloads at once [8] -> 
? govern uploads to the network's capacity [true] -> 
? TLS implementation (openssl, native) [openssl] -> 
? domain name -> docs
? versioning [true] -> 
? symlinks (keep, follow, skip) [keep] -> 
? read-only [false] -> 
? chunk size (blank: the store's) -> 
? cache chunk size (blank: default) -> 
? cache limit [1 GiB] -> 
? type (gcs, http-proxy, local, s3) [local] -> local
? backend name -> main
? role (main, replica, backfill, readOnly) [main] -> 
? Store root -> /srv/docs
? Verify chunk writes [true] -> 
    1. main (local, main)
? backends: a number to edit, [a]dd, [r]emove N, [d]one [d] -> 
? mount it as a folder on this machine (fuse) [yes] -> 
? fuse: other options [no] -> 
? serve it to other machines over HTTPS (http-proxy) [no] -> yes
? Port -> 5446
? TLS certificate -> 
? TLS key -> 
? Shared secret -> (secret)
? Serve share links [false] -> 
? http-proxy: other options [no] -> 
  Domains:
    1. docs: 1 backends
? a number to edit that domain, [a]dd, [r]emove N, [g]lobals, [w]rite, [q]uit -> w
new: would write
{
  "name": "laptop",
  "domains": [
    {
      "name": "docs",
      "versioning": true,
      "symlinks": "keep",
      "maxCache": "1 GiB",
      "backends": [
        {
          "type": "local",
          "name": "main",
          "role": "main",
          "path": "/srv/docs"
        }
      ],
      "frontends": [
        "fuse",
        {
          "type": "http-proxy",
          "port": 5446,
          "secret": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

== an existing config: what is not asked is kept, an unused link dropped
